        {
          "id": "f974323e70b54a95",
          "role": "A",
          "parent_id": null,
          "delegation_parent": "R/A",
          "integration_sources": [],
          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "A single contiguous rolling row, updated in place during the row-major scan, should improve locality and eliminate the per-row copy. Compact sorted obstacle positions should also avoid allocating an N×N blocked bitmap while preserving dense-DP work.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Replace the two rolling rows and row-copy loop with one in-place DP vector, using the previous-row value at dp[col] and current-row value at dp[col-1].",
              "Replace the nested blocked-cell bitmap with sorted, deduplicated linear cell positions scanned alongside the row-major DP."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
          "mean_seconds": 0.04899192973971367,
          "commit": "752e580b7b105cb0eb5be77f5f7fcff25e7c7daa"
        },
        {
          "id": "a6792f3d1b18447e",
          "role": "B",
          "parent_id": null,
          "delegation_parent": "R/B",
          "integration_sources": [],
          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Sweeping the grid by anti-diagonals makes cells within each wavefront independent: each reads only the preceding wavefront, so GCC can legally SIMD-vectorize the contiguous inner loops. Rolling wavefront buffers also remove the baseline's full blocked matrix and per-row copy.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Reordered the dynamic program into anti-diagonal wavefronts and used two rolling O(N) buffers, swapping rather than copying rows.",
              "Replaced the N×N blocked bitmap with sorted diagonal/row keys and O(N) timestamp storage.",
              "Marked dependency-free inner wavefront loops for GCC SIMD and replaced modulo operations on two reduced values with one conditional subtraction."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
          "mean_seconds": 0.008852349283794561,
          "commit": "5c79347481556dacf7d34eebc5b7ca8882f2002a"
        },
        {
          "id": "9748113282e34da1",
          "role": "C",
          "parent_id": null,
          "delegation_parent": "R/C",
          "integration_sources": [],
          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "For sufficiently large grids, work-sharing fixed column chunks can parallelize each row's prefix recurrence while retaining rolling-row memory; compact reset-or-add chunk summaries preserve the left-to-right dependency. Small grids avoid OpenMP scheduling overhead.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Replace the dense blocked-cell bitmap with sorted sparse obstacle columns per row.",
              "Use OpenMP static work-sharing to summarize and compute fixed-size row chunks; compose each chunk's reset-or-add summary in a row-level prefix pass.",
              "Keep a serial rolling-row path below a fixed size threshold and when OpenMP is unavailable."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
          "mean_seconds": 0.03673748020082712,
          "commit": "8a0d4ee8cc37eec194489c1ed3bea26a4fe955b7"
        },
        {
          "id": "11ed73a003f84a8a",
          "role": "A",
          "parent_id": null,
          "delegation_parent": "R/A",
          "integration_sources": [],
          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "A work-based hybrid should improve locality and avoid unnecessary dense-grid work: sparse obstacle coordinates use diagonal-order combinatorial counting, while denser cases use a contiguous, in-place row-major DP row instead of an N×N blocked bitmap and per-row copying.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Store blocked coordinates as a deduplicated O(M) vector and use first-hit binomial path counts when the obstacle-pair work is below a conservative N-based crossover.",
              "For denser cases, scan obstacles in row-major order alongside a single contiguous DP row, update it in place, and replace modulo operations with conditional reductions."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
          "mean_seconds": 0.049719556234776974,
          "commit": "6a830e91901299d4d55fd47e98b4c5f275a01f2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "36e61dc364844be3",
          "role": "B",
          "parent_id": "a6792f3d1b18447e",
          "delegation_parent": "R/B",
          "integration_sources": [],
          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "Computing each anti-diagonal without obstacle checks in the cell loop, then zeroing its sparse blocked positions, should reduce per-cell memory traffic and masking while leaving the independent recurrence loops easier for GCC to SIMD-vectorize.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Store blocked coordinates sorted by (anti-diagonal, row) rather than encoding them into a packed key.",
              "Remove the per-cell blocked-stamp array and compute each anti-diagonal with unmasked independent loops.",
              "After each diagonal is computed, zero all blocked positions on it before swapping buffers."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
          "mean_seconds": 0.00839559237162272,
          "commit": "d641a22d33dd4957c8e42169d3d3f83eb586c861"
        },
        {
          "id": "c320cf54ab8b4572",
          "role": "C",
          "parent_id": null,
          "delegation_parent": "R/C",
          "integration_sources": [],
          "hypothesis_as_declared_by_model": "A tiled diagonal wavefront exposes independent tile work while preserving the north/west path dependencies. For larger grids, static OpenMP work sharing across 32x32 tiles should amortize scheduling over useful work; rolling tile-edge buffers and sparse per-row obstacles avoid an N×N allocation. Small grids stay on a serial rolling-row path.",
          "transformations_as_declared_by_model": {
            "files": [
              "src/solution.cpp"
            ],
            "retained": [
              "Store blocked columns by row instead of allocating a dense N×N blocked-cell bitmap; use a serial rolling-row recurrence for n < 512.",
              "For larger grids, process 32×32 tiles in diagonal wavefront order, work-share each wave with OpenMP schedule(static), and retain only the preceding wave's bottom and right tile edges."
            ]
          },
          "status": "valid",
          "mean_seconds": 0.012753821288545927,
          "commit": "3a3defdde372ab75735b6f94cbc2f239a037e3b7"
        },
        {
          "id": "96fa93ec70334498",
          "role": "G",
